+++ b/docs/changes/brownfield-link-expiration.md
@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+# Change record: Brownfield: add link expiration to the existing service
+
+_Run `brownfield`. Generated by the docs agent._
+
+## Requirement (as stated)
+
+> Marketing wants campaign links that expire. When creating a short link, clients may set an optional expiry time. After that time the short link must stop redirecting and return 410 Gone, while its metadata and click analytics remain available. Links created without an expiry keep working forever, and the redirect path has to stay as fast as it is today.
+
+## Interpreted as
+
+- **Create short links** (stated (matched 'short link'))
+  - FR-1: A client can submit an absolute http(s) URL and receive a unique, non-guessable short code and short URL.
+  - FR-2: Invalid, unsafe or self-referencing destination URLs are rejected with a validation error.
+- **Redirect** (stated (matched 'redirect'))
+  - FR-3: Requesting a short code redirects the caller to the destination URL.
+- **Click analytics** (stated (matched 'analytics'))
+  - FR-4: Link owners can see total clicks, clicks per day and top referrers for a link.
+- **Link expiration** (stated (matched 'expire'))
+  - FR-5: A client may set an optional expiry time (ISO-8601 UTC) when creating a link; it must be in the future and at most 5 years ahead.
+  - FR-6: After expiry the short link stops redirecting and returns 410 Gone; expired visits are not counted as clicks.
+  - FR-7: Metadata and analytics of expired links remain available; links created without expiry never expire.
+
+## Assumptions
+
+- 'fast' interpreted as: Redirect p99 latency must not regress versus the current release (measured on the same hardware).
+
+## Plan
+
+- `T-expiry-domain` Expiry in domain model and service
+- `T-expiry-store` Persist expiry in the journal (backward compatible) (after ["T-expiry-domain"])
+- `T-expiry-api` expiresAt in the HTTP contract, 410 Gone (after ["T-expiry-domain"])
+- `T-expiry-tests` Expiry tests (service, API, journal compatibility) (after ["T-expiry-domain","T-expiry-store","T-expiry-api"])
+- reused existing: link_creation
+- reused existing: redirect
+- reused existing: click_analytics
+
+## API changes
+
+- POST /api/v1/links: new optional field expiresAt (additive, backward compatible)
+- GET /api/v1/links/{code}: response gains expiresAt (null when not set)
+- GET|HEAD /{code}: new status 410 gone for expired links
+
+## Data changes
+
+- journal 'link' record: optional expiresAt field; old records without it load as never-expiring (format version unchanged)
+
+## Risks
+
+- link_expiration: clock skew between instances could make expiry fire early or late by the skew - acceptable at second granularity
+- link_expiration: clients that cached a 302 keep redirecting after expiry - mitigated: redirects are sent with Cache-Control private, max-age=0
